  "preservation": [
    "Keep the three busy/None, not-busy/None and not-busy/Some outcomes, the shared private outcome model and full payloads; keep Tier 1E shared-file sequencing.",
    "QualityScheduler.ts:221-222,853-862 polls fs.exists until false every 25 ms, with a five-second timeout. Read errors conservatively continue as true; timeout returns true.",
    "Keep processReapClaim:905-912 and processPromotionTransition:1183-1190 pending-result errors. The observer neither takes over sinks nor removes pending records or releases another owner lock.",
    "Keep origin gate release on staging error/overshoot, admitted ownership handoff, transition-error release, pre-scan clock, masked promotion/restored sleep, sticky blocked clock and heartbeat order.",
    "Keep all ticket/lease/promotion/journal codecs, v1/v2/v3 compatibility, protocol-v2 fencing, full attribution, omission and once-per-owner sink semantics.",
    "The live fixture at quality-scheduler.test.ts:3319-3472 holds an injected sink, observes repeated claim checks and a pending observer after another second, then completes both fibers with exact event counts and empty lease/queue/claim directories.",
    "The complete earlier fixture prefix1-3318 and explicit ProcessIdentity compatibility span1902-1935 are byte-identical. Raw default identity and prefixed recorded replay stay supported.",
    "Current design test coordinates came from the R28 source; late citations require its earlier +48 and incoming +41, not a blanket +41. Exact endpoint mappings distinguish unchanged spans from prior fixture edits.",
    "The original 17-design stage and all its frozen evidence remain unchanged; this public companion documents the single accepted fixture equality exception."
  ],
